cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Evergreen Compose in research, benchmarks, or published work,
  please cite the software using this metadata.
title: Evergreen Compose
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Green
    given-names: Anthony
version: 0.0.1
date-released: "2026-10-04"
repository-code: https://github.com/atgreen/evergreen-compose
url: https://github.com/atgreen/evergreen-compose
# CFF 1.2 accepts individual SPDX license identifiers here, but not a `WITH`
# exception expression. The URL and abstract record the complete licensing
# arrangement: GPL-3.0-or-later WITH Classpath-exception-2.0.
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
license-url: https://github.com/atgreen/evergreen-compose#license
abstract: >-
  Evergreen Compose is an experimental toolkit for native Android applications
  written in Evergreen Common Lisp. Lisp describes UI trees, application state,
  and callbacks; a shared precompiled Jetpack Compose and Material 3 runtime
  handles layout, input, scrolling, and animation. Applications are packaged
  and signed with EGCL without a Java or Kotlin build toolchain. The toolkit
  is distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later with the Classpath Exception 2.0.
keywords:
  - Common Lisp
  - Android
  - Jetpack Compose
  - Material Design
  - user interfaces
